; daemon-vhc-completion.cddl — the async completion-result wire grammar (ABI companion §7.5).
;
; The `completion-result` is the decoded content of an `Event::Completion(op, result)` (event tag 6,
; ABI §4.2/§4.6) and of a `completion-rec.result` byte string (journal tag 14, §8.3). The journal
; stores it OPAQUELY as a `bstr`; this grammar is the normative shape of those bytes. Per ABI §7.5
; the encoding is "fixed now" — before any completion is linked (Phase B) — precisely so journals
; and SDKs are stable across the phase that makes it real. It lives verbatim in `daemon-vhc-abi`
; (the shared contracts ground), MUST validate as-is under `cddl-cat`, and the `completion_grammar`
; test asserts it is machine-valid and that a representative of each variant validates.
;
; The result-variant set is additive within major 2 (ABI §1.4); unknown `comp-error` codes fail
; closed (§5.2). Note on byte lengths: matching journal.cddl / daemon-swarm.cddl, `cddl-cat` parses
; but does not enforce `.size N`; the fixed-width `bstr .size 32` (a blake3 content hash) carries its
; size verbatim from the spec (the Rust codec enforces the actual length).

completion-result = [0, success-payload]      ; success (COMPLETION_RESULT_OK)
                  / [1, comp-error]            ; failure (COMPLETION_RESULT_ERR)

; A success carries exactly one of: an opaque handle (buffer/tensor/stream — kind-tagged per §7.2),
; a 32-byte content hash (the payload_put commitment), or unit (stream_write / publish-ack / a
; cancel whose target had no result).
success-payload = uint                         ; a handle (buffer/tensor/stream), kind-tagged §7.2
                / bstr .size 32                ; a content hash (payload_put)
                / null                         ; unit success (stream_write, publish-ack, cancel-target)

comp-error = {
  "code":   uint,      ; 0 = Cancelled, 1 = NetUnreachable, 2 = Timeout, 3 = StoreRefused,
                       ; 4 = HashMismatch, 5 = CreditExhausted, 6 = PeerClosed,
                       ; 7 = GrantExhausted, 8 = DeviceError (compute@2 deferred device error,
                       ; the C1 compute-minor addition); 9..=63 reserved (additive by minor)
  ? "detail": tstr,
}
